<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guan Daosheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1262">1262</a>–1319</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Guan Zhongji, Lady Zhongji, Kuan Tao-sheng</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guan Daosheng was a Chinese painter, calligrapher and poet of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a>, credited as the most famous female painter and calligrapher in Chinese history and a prominent figure in bamboo painting. Born into a landed family in Huzhou, she married the scholar-official and artist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-mengfu">Zhao Mengfu</a> in 1286 and travelled with him between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a> and the south. Her ink bamboo, unusual for a woman because the plant carried masculine associations, set bamboo within misty landscapes; the Yuan court collected her work and in 1317 gave her the title Madam of the Wei Kingdom. She died in 1319, and a handscroll of 1308 in the National Palace Museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taipei">Taipei</a> has a plausible claim to be hers.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The painter <b>Guan Daosheng</b>, wife of Zhao Mengfu, won fame of her own.</blockquote><a href="/societies/yuan-china">Social Hierarchy of Yuan China</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Huzhou, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=30.89,120.09&amp;year=1299" aria-label="Huzhou on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7657 1037 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Guan Daosheng"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8107 1307h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8107 1307h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=30.89,120.09&amp;year=1299">What was here in 1299? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
